          "beacon:entityType": "METHOD"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "ubiquitin-proteasome system",
          "beacon:entityType": "METHOD"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:predicate": "relates_to",
          "beacon:object": "autophagy",
          "beacon:evidence": "misregulated protein breakdown mechanisms involved, such as autophagy"
        },
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:predicate": "relates_to",
          "beacon:object": "ubiquitin-proteasome system",
          "beacon:evidence": "misregulated protein breakdown mechanisms involved, such as... ubiquitin-proteasome system"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-ctarc-2025-100913-sec0008-p4",
      "beacon:sectionType": "other",
      "schema:text": "This subsection from a study on ferroptosis explores the morphological features that differentiate it from apoptosis, necrosis, and autophagy, highlighting changes like mild chromatin condensation and cytoplasmic swelling.\n\n### Morphological features\n\nIn terms of morphology, biochemistry, and genetics, ferroptosis is distinct from apoptosis, necrosis, and autophagy, according to a preliminary study. Many researchers agree that cells going through ferroptosis typically exhibit morphological alterations resembling necrosis [ 92 ]. These characteristics include mild chromatin condensation, cytoplasmic swelling (oncosis), loss of plasma membrane integrity, and enlargement of cytoplasmic organelles. Ferroptosis can occasionally be accompanied by increased autophagosomes, as well as the detachment and rounding up of cells. Notably, ferroptosis that starts in one cell has the ability to rapidly propagate to neighboring cells [ 85 ].",
      "schema:name": "Ferroptosis",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "Morphological features",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:entityType": "CONCEPT"
        },
        {
