        },
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "mevalonate pathway",
          "beacon:predicate": "contradicts",
          "beacon:object": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:evidence": "Reduced selenocysteine tRNA synthesis, decreased GPX4 activity, and ferroptosis are the results of inhibiting the MVA pathway"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-ctarc-2025-100913-sec0014-p5",
      "beacon:sectionType": "other",
      "schema:text": "This subsection from the article discusses how inhibiting the MVA pathway leads to ferroptosis by reducing selenocysteine tRNA synthesis and GPX4 activity, highlighting the role of system Xc- in cellular antioxidant processes.\n\nReduced selenocysteine tRNA synthesis, decreased GPX4 activity, and ferroptosis are the results of inhibiting the MVA pathway [ 52 ]. ### Inducing Ferroptosis by suppressing system XC\n\nSystem Xc- is a widely distributed amino acid anti-transporter in phospholipid bilayers. It is a heterodimer that is engaged in a significant antioxidant process in the cell, and it is made up of the SLC7A11 and SLC3A2 subunits [ 52 ]. Glutamate and cysteine are moved into and out of cells in a 1:1 ratio by machine Xc-. Cysteine that enters cells is transformed into cysteine, which is then utilized to produce glutathione (GSH) [ 49 ]. Under the direction of glutathione peroxidases, GSH reduces reactive oxygen species and nitrogen dioxide (GPXs). By preventing cystine absorption, inhibiting system Xc-activity lowers GSH production [ 52 ]. This ultimately results in a decrease in GPX activity, a decrease in the antioxidant capacity of cells, a build-up of lipid reactive oxygen species, oxidative damage, and ferroptosis. By downregulating SLC7A11 expression, P53 can also reduce lipid ROS accumulation, ferroptosis, and the antioxidant ability of cells and interfering with GPX4 action. This leads to a decline in ferroptosis, lipid ROS accumulation, and cell antioxidant capacity [ 79 ].",
      "schema:name": "Mechanisms of Ferroptosis and Cancer Therapy",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "Inducing Ferroptosis by suppressing system XC",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "MVA pathway",
          "beacon:entityType": "CONCEPT"
        },
        {
