    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-ctarc-2025-100913-sec0022-p3",
      "beacon:sectionType": "other",
      "schema:text": "This other section from the article discusses the synergistic effects of combining ferroptosis inducers with immune checkpoint inhibitors or radiotherapy in preclinical studies, as well as ongoing translational studies evaluating the safety and efficacy of these therapies in clinical trials.\n\nAdditionally, combination therapies, such as ferroptosis inducers with immune checkpoint inhibitors or radiotherapy, have shown synergistic effects in preclinical settings (Tang et al., 2021; Stockwell et al., 2020). Translational studies are underway to evaluate the safety and efficacy of ferroptosis-targeted therapies in clinical trials. While still in early stages, some clinical trials have been initiated to explore the potential of ferroptosis inducers in cancer patients. These studies aim to determine the optimal dosing, safety profiles, and preliminary efficacy of these agents. Biomarkers, such as GPX4 expression and iron levels, are being investigated to identify patients who may benefit most from ferroptosis-based therapies (Lei et al., 2023). The transition from preclinical to clinical application is a critical step in realizing the therapeutic potential of ferroptosis.",
      "schema:name": "Ferroptosis regulation and its Role in Physiological Conditions",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "Preclinical evidence and translational studies on ferroptosis in Cancer therapy",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:entityType": "CONCEPT"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
