    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-ctarc-2025-100913-sec0024-p0",
      "beacon:sectionType": "other",
      "schema:text": "This morphological indications section from the article discusses the cell shrinkage and mitochondrial changes observed in ferroptotic cells, highlighting their unique characteristics compared to apoptosis.\n\n### Morphological Indications\n\nCell Shrinkage : Unlike apoptosis, which often involves cell fragmentation into apoptotic bodies, ferroptotic cells typically exhibit cell shrinkage and reduced cell volume [ 74 ]. Mitochondrial Changes : Mitochondria in ferroptotic cells often show specific alterations, such as a reduction in mitochondrial membrane density, smaller and more elongated shapes, and the absence of cristae or damaged cristae [ 58 ]. Membrane Rupture : Cells undergoing ferroptosis may display plasma membrane damage or rupture, although this is less prominent compared to necrosis [ 72 ].",
      "schema:name": "Morphological and biochemical indications of Ferroptosis",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "Morphological Indications",
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "ferroptotic cells",
          "beacon:predicate": "produces",
          "beacon:object": "cell shrinkage",
          "beacon:evidence": "ferroptotic cells typically exhibit cell shrinkage and reduced cell volume"
        },
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "ferroptotic cells",
          "beacon:predicate": "produces",
          "beacon:object": "mitochondrial changes",
          "beacon:evidence": "Mitochondria in ferroptotic cells often show specific alterations"
        },
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "ferroptotic cells",
          "beacon:predicate": "supports",
          "beacon:object": "plasma membrane damage",
          "beacon:evidence": "Cells undergoing ferroptosis may display plasma membrane damage or rupture"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-ctarc-2025-100913-sec0024-p1",
      "beacon:sectionType": "other",
      "schema:text": "This subsection from the article discusses biochemical indications of ferroptosis, focusing on membrane rupture and lipid peroxidation as key markers in the process.\n\nMembrane Rupture : Cells undergoing ferroptosis may display plasma membrane damage or rupture, although this is less prominent compared to necrosis [ 72 ]. ### Biochemical Indications\n\nLipid Peroxidation : The build-up of oxidized lipids, especially in polyunsaturated fatty acids, is a hallmark of ferroptosis. This can be measured using specific assays like the detection of malondialdehyde (MDA) or 4-hydroxy-2-nonenal (4-HNE) [ 64 ]. Reduced Glutathione Levels : Ferroptotic cells often exhibit decreased levels of glutathione (GSH), a crucial antioxidant that helps protect against oxidative stress [ 40 ].",
      "schema:name": "Morphological and biochemical indications of Ferroptosis",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "Biochemical Indications",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:entityType": "CONCEPT"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "malondialdehyde",
          "beacon:entityType": "ENTITY"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "4-hydroxy-2-nonenal",
          "beacon:entityType": "ENTITY"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "glutathione",
          "beacon:entityType": "ENTITY"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:predicate": "associated_with",
          "beacon:object": "membrane rupture",
          "beacon:evidence": "Cells undergoing ferroptosis may display plasma membrane damage or rupture"
        },
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:predicate": "associated_with",
          "beacon:object": "lipid peroxidation",
          "beacon:evidence": "The build-up of oxidized lipids... is a hallmark of ferroptosis"
        },
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
