    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-ctarc-2025-100913-sec0028-p2",
      "beacon:sectionType": "other",
      "schema:text": "This novel drug delivery systems section from the article discusses the synergistic effects of combining ferroptosis inducers with doxorubicin and immunotherapy in overcoming drug resistance and enhancing anti-tumor immune responses in cancer therapy.\n\nFor example, combining ferroptosis inducers with doxorubicin has demonstrated synergistic effects in breast cancer models, suggesting that ferroptosis can be exploited to overcome drug resistance [ 16 ]. Furthermore, the integration of ferroptosis inducers with immunotherapy is being explored, as the immunogenic nature of ferroptosis may enhance anti-tumor immune responses [ 105 ]. This combination approach could revolutionize cancer treatment paradigms, offering new avenues for patients with refractory tumors.",
      "schema:name": "Novel Drug Delivery Systems Targeting Ferroptosis in Cancer Therapy and Clinical Implications",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
