      "schema:name": "Figure 1",
      "schema:caption": "Global cancer Incidence (Globocan 2018)",
      "schema:text": "Figure 1: Global cancer incidence reached approximately 18.1 million cases in 2018, with prostate, lung, and colorectal cancers representing the most commonly diagnosed types. The data demonstrates a significant global burden of cancer, underscoring the urgent need for innovative therapeutic approaches like ferroptosis in cancer treatment.\n\nCaption: Global cancer Incidence (Globocan 2018)",
