    {
      "@type": "schema:ImageObject",
      "beacon:chunkId": "fig0002",
      "schema:name": "Figure 2",
      "schema:caption": "Basic ferroptosis pathway. Created from biorender.com",
      "schema:text": "Figure 2: The basic ferroptosis pathway is regulated by several key mechanisms, including the inhibition of cystine-glutamate antiporter system Xc-, which decreases glutathione levels and leads to lipid peroxidation. The activation of GPX4 has been identified as a crucial player in suppressing ferroptosis by converting lipid hydroperoxides to non-toxic lipid alcohols. This pathway highlights the potential of targeting ferroptosis in cancer therapy to induce cell death in cancer cells that are resistant to conventional treatments.\n\nCaption: Basic ferroptosis pathway. Created from biorender.com",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "ferroptosis",
          "beacon:entityType": "CONCEPT"
