  "schema:table": [
    {
      "@type": "schema:Table",
      "beacon:chunkId": "tbl0001",
      "schema:name": "Table 1",
      "schema:caption": "Comparison of Cell Death Mechanisms",
      "schema:text": "Table 1: Ferroptosis has a high role in cancer therapy compared to necrosis, which has no role, and both apoptosis and pyroptosis, which have some role. Ferroptosis is dependent on iron, while apoptosis and necrosis show no such dependency. The table demonstrates that ferroptosis is a promising mechanism for advancing cancer therapy strategies.\n\nCaption: Comparison of Cell Death Mechanisms\n\n| Feature | Apoptosis | Necrosis | Ferroptosis | Pyroptosis | Autophagy |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cell Shrinkage | Yes | No | Yes | No | No |\n| Membrane Rupture | No | Yes | Yes | Yes | No |\n| Inflammatory Response | No | Yes | Yes | Yes | No |\n| Dependency on Iron | No | No | Yes | No | No |\n| Role in Cancer Therapy | Some | None | High | Some | Some |"
    }
  ]
}